{
 "id": "keepalive/ping/minimum-lifetime/no-rescue",
 "description": "OpenAI GPT-5.6: the entry lifetime is a 30-minute minimum, not a proven expiry (R45). A ping at minute 30 reads the 11,060 tokens, and the next request arrives at minute 35 and reads them too. A gap past a minimum proves nothing, so the phase is unknown until the read in the usage proves the entry: it becomes hot. A rescue claims the entry would have expired, which a minimum cannot show, so none is credited and the window is only the ping's cost, 11,060 x $0.30 + 10 x $3.00 + $15.00 per million = -$0.00336. mask's 5,940 tokens are read, not written: +$0.00178.",
